# Dated one-time events (Phase 8D.2; docs/evaluation/phase-8a/03-schema-and-temporal.md §3, option C). Additive only: one
# concrete type under the `event` slot core/0001 left abstract, and one attribute. No existing type, attribute or data
# changes, so no existing claim, id or proposition key changes.
#
# An event happened at some instant inside [occurred-at-earliest, occurred-at-latest). It has no valid time: it never
# "holds", so it can never enter spell assembly. Both bounds are absent for an event stated with no date; none is invented.
# When something was SAID is the observation's time, which is a separate thing.
#
# - occurred-at-basis: "stated" (the text gives the date) or "derived" (read from the time the message was written, as in
#   "last week" or a month with no year).
# - Roles and predicate mirror `statement`, so one extractor contract covers both.

define
  attribute occurred-at-basis, value string @values("stated", "derived");
  relation event-statement sub event,
    relates subject @card(1..), relates object @card(0..),
    owns predicate-text, owns object-text, owns occurred-at-basis;
  referent plays event-statement:subject, plays event-statement:object;
